        <body>
            <div xml:id="d206">

                <pb facs="0411" n="1065" sameAs="frus:frus1875v02/pg1065"/>

                <head>No. 505.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Schuyler to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1875-05-15"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 15, 1875</date>.
                        (Received June 3.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 116.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that a
                    treaty has been concluded between Russia and Japan, by which Russia cedes to
                    Japan the Kurile <pb facs="0412" n="1066" xml:id="pg1066"/> Islands, in exchange
                    for all the rights of Japan to the island of Saghalien.]</p>
                <p>I understand that the treaty has already been ratified by the Emperor of
                    Russia.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>EUGENE SCHUYLER.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
